{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 47, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "Hark to thee good traveler who dost yearn to tread\nThe sacred sands and emerald paths of Japan fair\nLo here lies thy journey penn’d in verse most grand\nA pilgrimage through time and wonder to explore\n\nUpon thy first morn in that land of rising sun\nDo thou awake in fair Tokyo where marvels lie\nTo the tower tall of Tokyo’s skyline bold\nAscend to view a city ‘neath the dawn’s soft glow\n\nNext bid thou adieu to steel and stone so grand\nAnd venture forth to Asakusa’s streets so old\nThere visit the temple where Kannon dwells in grace\nAnd buy a fortune from a stall with colors bright\n\nOn thy second day journey to the shrine of Meiji\nWhere ancient gods and modern life do intertwine\nThen stroll through Harajuku where fashion doth reign\nAnd quaff the matcha sweet at a café most fine\n\nLo now thy path leads to the land of ancient lore\nThe city of Kyoto where history doth sleep\nBegin at Fushimi Inari where torii gates ascend\nA path of vermilion that doth the soul enthrall\n\nThen wander to Kinkaku-ji where gold doth gleam\nUpon the pond where reflections dance and play\nVisit Gion where geisha ghosts in lantern light\nDo glide like phantoms through the evening’s gentle spray\n\nOn thy third morn take heed and hasten thou\nTo Nara’s deer who in the parks do graze and play\nFeed them from thy hand as they with gentle noses nudge\nThen gaze upon the Great Buddha in its hall so vast\n\nReturn thou now to Kyoto for one final night\nDine on kaiseki where each dish a masterpiece\nThen rest thy head for morn shall break anew\n\nAwake and take thy leave of Kyoto’s storied streets\nTo Hiroshima where peace and memory collide\nAt the park of peace stand solemn in reflection\nWhere souls lost in war beneath the dome do lie\n\nThen on to Miyajima where the floating torii stands\nA gate of time that doth defy the rising tide\nWitness the seto’s bridge where legends old are spun\nAnd eat the famous oysters raw by seashore wide\n\nNow thou must turn thy steps toward Osaka’s cheer\nWhere street food sizzles on a thousand stalls\nTry the takoyaki balls and okonomiyaki too\nThen ride the train to Osaka Castle’s walls\n\nBehold the final day draws nigh and Tokyo calls\nTo Shibuya’s scramble where the world doth race\nThen cross the river to the shrine of Meiji once more\nBefore thy flight home at Narita’s vast embrace\n\nSo ends thy tale a journey through Japan’s embrace\nWhere ancient whispers and the future intertwine\nMay thy heart be light and thy soul feel the grace\nOf this fair isle where wonders never cease to shine.", "logprobs": [{"token": "H", "logprob": -0.1340528428554535}, {"token": "ark", "logprob": -0.004188099876046181}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -2.6293089389801025}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.04873698577284813}, {"token": "e", "logprob": -0.0028606229461729527}, {"token": " good", "logprob": -3.0002994537353516}, {"token": " travel", "logprob": -0.5407403707504272}, {"token": "er", "logprob": -0.0008506731828674674}, {"token": " who", "logprob": -1.943387508392334}, {"token": " dost", "logprob": -0.24399428069591522}, {"token": " year", "logprob": -3.2900965213775635}, {"token": "n", "logprob": -0.001613625674508512}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -0.44121015071868896}, {"token": " tread", "logprob": -0.3934767246246338}, {"token": "\n", "logprob": -0.2432437241077423}, {"token": "The", "logprob": -0.7501625418663025}, {"token": " sacred", "logprob": -1.561166763305664}, {"token": " sands", "logprob": -1.8955587148666382}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -1.2196762561798096}, {"token": " emer", "logprob": -2.800713539123535}, {"token": "ald", "logprob": -0.0003494605771265924}, {"token": " paths", "logprob": -1.8728358745574951}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.6758170127868652}, {"token": " Japan", "logprob": -1.1602110862731934}, {"token": " fair", "logprob": -1.1447622776031494}, {"token":